# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Custom Disc — public repository
#
# How this repository gets populated: the five non-source files in this folder
# (this file, LICENSE, .gitattributes, and .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*) are
# uploaded ONCE through the GitHub web interface. No local git repository is
# connected to this folder, and the mod jar is attached to GitHub Releases by
# hand for each version.
#
# The rules below are therefore a SAFETY NET, not an active mechanism. They are
# here so that if a local repository is ever connected to this folder, the
# source code cannot be committed by accident.
#
# ===========================================================================
#  WARNING: "git add -f <file>" bypasses every rule in this file.
#  If a local repository is ever connected here, never use "git add -f".
# ===========================================================================
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Source code: must never reach the public repository ----
# Extension rules are deliberate: a directory-only rule such as "src/" would
# NOT catch a single stray .java file sitting loose in the project root.
*.java
*.kt
*.kts
*.gradle.kts
*.class
src/

# ---- Gradle / build scaffolding ----
.gradle/
gradle/
gradlew
gradlew.bat
*.gradle
gradle.properties
build/
out/
classes/

# ---- Development runtime ----
# Contains the dev worlds, logs, and the audio files imported into discs.
run/

# ---- Built artifacts ----
# The mod jar is distributed through GitHub Releases, not through the repo tree.
*.jar

# ---- GitHub Actions ----
# build.yml cannot run here: the source it builds is not published. Ignoring it
# prevents a permanently failing check on the public repository.
# Delete this rule if you ever decide to publish the source.
.github/workflows/

# ---- IDE ----
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.settings/
.vscode/
bin/
.classpath
.project
*.launch

# ---- OS ----
*.DS_Store
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- JVM crash / profiling dumps ----
hs_err_*.log
replay_*.log
*.hprof
*.jfr
